   "subject": "Re: [Israel RUG] convert nested list of html into nested list in r",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">look at this code - it converts an html to a nested list, named by element names<div><br></div><div>require(&quot;XML&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>root = xmlRoot(htmlParse(&quot;your file name here&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div><div>html2list =function(root) {</div><div>  result = list()</div><div>  name = xmlName(root)</div><div>  sublist = lapply(xmlChildren(root),html2list)</div><div>  result[[name]] = sublist</div><div>  result</div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><div>nested.list = html2list(root)</div><div><br></div><div>I didn&#39;t thoroughly debug it, but I give the code just to show the direction.</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
